  <content>
  <section>
<div class="os-raise-familysupport">
  <para>Access the <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b62c9150250bf52d6cc37569213ab516e0090dca">Desmos guide PDF</link> for tips on solving problems with the Desmos graphing calculator.</para>
</div>

<para>For questions 1 - 2, write an equation in vertex form of the quadratic function that has a vertex at (5, 8) and also goes through the point \((-3, 6)\).</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="58610f1c-5083-4788-b112-383c4e6b3229"><problem><para>
      <para> Find the value of \(a\) for vertex form. </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>-1/32</para><para>
      <para>Nice try! The correct answer is \(\frac{-1}{32}\).</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<!--Q#2-->
<!--Q#2-->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> Write the equation in vertex form. </para>
    <para>Enter your answer here and select the <emphasis>Solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(y=\frac{-1}{32}(x-5)^2+8\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>
<para>For questions 3 and 4, write an equation in vertex form of the quadratic function that has a vertex at \((-4, 3)\) and also goes through the point \((2, 5)\).</para>
<!--Interaction End -->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="3fb8876e-eb1f-4f46-99ef-2345f1eefa1b"><problem><para>
      <para> Find the value of \(a\) for vertex form. </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>1/18</para><para>
      <para>Nice try! The correct answer is \(\frac{1}{18}\).</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<!--Q#4-->
<!--Q#4-->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> Write the equation in vertex form. </para>
    <para>Enter your answer here and select the <emphasis>Solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(y=\frac{1}{18}(x+4)^2+3\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>
<!--Interaction End -->

<para>For questions 5 - 6, write an equation in vertex form of the quadratic function that has a vertex at \((6, -2)\) and also goes through the point \((3, 1)\).</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="672d6cf9-11c0-41b0-8896-377ea42f89d5"><problem><para>
      <para> Find the value of \(a\) for vertex form. </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>1/3</para><para>
      <para>Nice try! The correct answer is \(\frac{1}{3}\).</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<!--Q#6-->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> Write the equation in vertex form. </para>
    <para>Enter your answer here and select the <emphasis>Solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(y=\frac{1}{3}(x-6)^2-2\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>
<!--Interaction End -->


